\f0\fs24 \cf0 Dataset: training_routes_100_with_coordinates.csv\
\
Purpose:\
This dataset contains 100 diverse railway routes for the development of an energy consumption model.\
\
Preparation:\
- Routes were selected to represent different regions of Germany.\
- Different geographical directions are included:\
  N-S, E-W, NE-SW, NW-SE.\
- Different route lengths are included:\
  short, medium, long.\
- Station data was cleaned and S-Bahn stations were filtered where possible.\
- DS100 station identifiers were retained for API queries.\
\
Columns:\
\
start_DS100:\
Unique identifier of the starting station\
\
start_name:\
Name of the starting station\
\
start_longitude / start_latitude:\
Coordinates of the starting station\
\
start_region:\
Regional classification of the starting station\
\
end_DS100:\
Unique identifier of the destination station\
\
end_name:\
Name of the destination station\
\
end_longitude / end_latitude:\
Coordinates of the destination station\
\
end_region:\
Regional classification of the destination station\
\
axis:\
Geographical direction of the route\
\
distance_category:\
Classification of route length (short/medium/long)\
\
air_distance_km:\
Straight-line distance between start and destination station\
\
Next step:\
Use the DS100 identifiers to query the Trassenfinder API and enrich the dataset with railway-specific route parameters and energy consumption values.}